																								<r3d:remarks>description: CFADC&#039;s mission is to compile, evaluate, recommend, and disseminate atomic and molecular collision data relevant to fusion energy research and development. Under different names, it has been a data center since 1958. Key features include a categorized bibliography of atomic and molecular collision references relevant to fusion energy and ALADDIN, a database management system accepted by the International Atomic Energy Agency for the exchange of atomic and molecular data. 
In 1970 the Atomic and Molecular Processes Information Center (AMPIC) became the Controlled Fusion Atomic Data Center (CFADC). 
Gateway to Research Data: http://dr-dn.cisti-icist.nrc-cnrc.gc.ca/eng/home/collection/Gateway%20to%20Research%20Data/</r3d:remarks>
